  "summary": "A piston pump moves liquid with a piston that slides in a cylinder liner, sealed against the bore by elastomer cups on the piston itself. In the double-acting design shown, both faces of the piston work: as it travels one way, the chamber ahead of it discharges while the chamber behind it fills, and the roles reverse on the return stroke. Two cylinders cranked 90° apart (duplex) give four deliveries per revolution. Used for drilling mud, slurries and general high-pressure transfer at moderate pressures.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Positive displacement – reciprocating",
    "configuration": "Horizontal, duplex, double-acting piston, crank-driven"
  },
  "model_configuration": {
    "cylinders": 2,
    "stroke_mm": 100.0,
    "liner_bore_mm": 100.0,
    "crank_phasing": "90°",
    "flow_formula": "Q ≈ n_cyl × [2·(π/4)D² − (π/4)d_rod²] × stroke × N × ηv (double-acting)"
  },
